# The two 64-bit UBWC compat types on A740: one cell of the compressor, measured

# Question: fd6_ubwc_compat_mode() answers FD6_UBWC_R16G16B16A16_INT for five members
#           of the 64-bit compatibility class and FD6_UBWC_R32G32_INT for three.  Is
#           that difference a property of the compressor on this chip, or a label
#           nobody ever tested?  It is the only reason a strict reading of upstream's
#           `TODO: limit based on compatiblity class` still refuses the class once the
#           members the driver cannot lay out are excluded
#           (results/model-strict-class-nolist.txt), and the class is 650.8 MiB of the
#           game's no-list bytes (journal 28).
# Method:   probe XMC in tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c.  A 512x512 image, 8 bytes a
#           texel, filled by vkCmdCopyBufferToImage with a pattern whose every eighth
#           word is one of the values upstream calls special (0, all ones, 1,
#           0x80008000, ...), read back twice by compute texelFetch through a
#           usampler2D: once as R16G16B16A16_UINT (four 16-bit halves) and once as
#           R32G32_UINT (two 32-bit words).  Both views are legal because both
#           families are named in the image's format list.
#           UBWC cannot be given to such a create today - the list mixes the two
#           labels, which is exactly the rule under test - so the driver carries the
#           experiment knob TU_UBWC_64B_MIX of experiments/exp-22-ubwc-64b-mix-knob.patch,
#           which folds the one label into the other and nothing else.  One binary, two
#           runs; the knob-off run is the control of the knob-on run, and the released
#           driver is the control for both.
# Tool:     tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test, sha256 5f44a7f7e6ae... in all three runs
# Drivers:  A build/p14-shipped/libvulkan_freedreno.so, sha256 c17d02bcaae9a960...  (the
#             released stack, no knob in it)
#           B build/out-exp22/libvulkan_freedreno.so, sha256 0e934fc6b3e0... (0001..0013
#             + exp-14 + exp-21 + exp-22, run with the knob off)
#           C the same .so as B, run with TU_UBWC_64B_MIX=1
#           (0014 is deliberately not applied: results/test-exp21-equiv-p14.log shows
#           that stack behaving like the released one)
# Device:   Adreno A740 (chip_id 0x43050a01), KMD msm
# Runs:     21.11, all three exit 0
# Command:  source scripts/env.sh && RP6_TEST_BIN=/tmp/opencode/testbuild-xmc/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test \
#               scripts/run-test.sh <icd> <log>       (and TU_UBWC_64B_MIX=1 for C)
# Raw:      results/raw/xmc-p14-noknob.log, results/raw/xmc-exp22-knoboff.log,
#           results/raw/xmc-exp22-knobon.log (gitignored)
#
=== 1. what the knob changed in the WHOLE log, not only in XMC ===
run A (released) against run B (same stack, knob off): 0 lines differ, of 621
run B against run C (the knob switched on):     2 log lines differ (the `diff` that
             prints them is 8 output lines: two hunks, each with its `---` separator)
the two lines run C differs by, in full:
    < XMC[MIX42 ] base R16G16B16A16_UINT list 2: opt=0x200000 lin=0x200000 raw=0x200000 tail=0x0 sparse=yes -> tiled (only a tiled image can be sparse)
    > XMC[MIX42 ] base R16G16B16A16_UINT list 2: opt=0x202000 lin=0x200000 raw=0x200000 tail=0x2000 sparse=yes -> tiled (size)
    < XMC[MIX24 ] base R32G32_UINT       list 2: opt=0x200000 lin=0x200000 raw=0x200000 tail=0x0 sparse=yes -> tiled (only a tiled image can be sparse)
    > XMC[MIX24 ] base R32G32_UINT       list 2: opt=0x202000 lin=0x200000 raw=0x200000 tail=0x2000 sparse=yes -> tiled (size)
  Everything else in the log - probes B/C/D/E/F/N/V/W/G/H/K, the trigger matrix,
  NL, XV, UBR, GEOM, CPU-FILL, CEIL and every readback row - is identical with the
  knob on.  Widening the 64-bit pair moves nothing else in the driver's behaviour.

